  "hints": [
    "Try starting from every cell that matches the first letter.",
    "Depth-first search with backtracking: mark a cell as used, explore the four neighbors for the next letter, then unmark it.",
    "def dfs(r, c, k):\n    if k == len(word): return true\n    if out of bounds or used or board[r][c] != word[k]: return false\n    mark used\n    found = any(dfs(nr, nc, k+1) for each neighbor)\n    unmark\n    return found",
    "Worst case O(cells \u00d7 3^L) for a word of length L, since each step has at most three new directions. Unmarking on the way back is what lets other paths reuse the cell."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(m n 3^L)",
    "space": "O(L)"
  },
